<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>FL2024- exam 23</title>
<style>
body { font-family: Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; }
h1 { color: #C0392B; font-size: 20pt; }
h2 { color: #1F618D; font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 24px; }
.qtext { font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 8px; white-space: pre-wrap; }
.opt { margin: 4px 0 4px 20px; }
.correct { color: green; font-weight: bold; }
.selectedwrong { color: red; font-weight: bold; }
.selectedright { color: green; font-weight: bold; }
.explain { background: #F4F6F6; padding: 8px; margin-top: 8px; font-style: italic; }
.video { margin-top:6px; }
img { max-width: 500px; margin: 10px 0; display:block; }
</style></head><body><h1>FL2024- EXAM 23 - Ket qua &amp; giai thich</h1><p><b>Ho ten:</b> Hang Tran<br/><b>Ket qua:</b> 5/31<br/><b>Thoi gian lam bai:</b> 47 giây<br/><b>Nop bai:</b> 2026-08-03T08:50:40.192Z</p><hr/><h2>Cau hoi 1</h2><div class="qtext">During which stage of the fundamental test process is the testability of requirements evaluated?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. Test Design. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. B. Test Analysis. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. C. Test Execution.</div><div class="opt ">d. D. Test Planning.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.4.1 đánh giá khả năng test của requirement là của Analysis</div><h2>Cau hoi 2</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is an approach that can be used for exploratory testing?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. A tester analyses, designs and implements tests based on external rules and standards. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. A tester methodically executes tests from a list of possible failures, based on experience, defect and failure data.</div><div class="opt correct">c. C. Time-boxed test sessions are created, during which a tester uses a test charter containing test objectives to guide the testing. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. D. Tests are designed based on the guidance of stakeholders and experts outside the test team.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.4.2 Exploratory Testing thì ra đáp án C đúng. A sai vì "external rules and standards" là checklist based, B sai vì "based on experience, defect and failure data" là của error guessing, D sai vì "guidance of stakeholders and experts outside" là của Consultative mục 5.2.2</div><h2>Cau hoi 3</h2><div class="qtext">A car insurance policy has 3 rates of insurance depending on the age of the driver. For drivers aged between 17 and 25 inclusive they are charged at rate A, drivers aged between 26 and 50 inclusive are charged at rate B and those drivers aged over 50 are charged at rate C. You are designing test cases, which of the following three ages would test all valid equivalence partitions and therefore test rate A, B and C?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. 17, 25, 50. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. 10, 21, 55.</div><div class="opt correct">c. C. 20, 35, 65. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. D. 26, 45, 50.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2.1 Vẽ ra nhé</div><h2>Cau hoi 4</h2><div class="qtext">You are performing a review, how many comments do you find based on checklist? The Test Cases are as follows: TC1. Success - valid 'User Name' and 'Password'; Customer Menu displayed TC2. Failure - 'User Name' field has blank entry; Error Number 12 displayed TC3. Failure - 'User Id' entered does not exist on database (i.e. unregistered user); Error Number 23 displayed TC4. Failure - 'Password' entered does not match user's password on database; Error Number 24 displayed You are guided by the following checklist in your review: C1. There must be one test case to cover success C2. There must be one test case for each error path ( validation failure) C3. Each test case must use terminology consistent with the test basis document (field names, error number)</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. 1. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. 2.</div><div class="opt correct">c. C. 3. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. D. 4.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.2 Câu hỏi là bạn tìm đc bao nhiêu comments dựa vào checklist khi review test case của đồng nghiệp. Comment gồm có: TC1, TC3 bị sai vì "Customer Menu" và "'User Id' không có trong màn hình đặc tả, và thiếu 1 test case cho trường hợp Blank password</div><h2>Cau hoi 5</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following are triggers for Maintenance testing? a) System migration from one platform to another. b) Retirement of a system. c) Preparation for an audit of a system. d) Modifications to a system. e) Development of a whole new system.</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. a, c and d. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. a, d and e.</div><div class="opt ">c. C. b, c and e.</div><div class="opt correct">d. D. a, b and d. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.4.1 Triggers for Maintenance: Modification- Migration -Retirement</div><h2>Cau hoi 6</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following BEST describes a Test Case?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. A testable aspect of a component or system identified as a basis for testing. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. A description of the test objectives to be achieved and the means and the schedule for achieving them.</div><div class="opt correct">c. C. A set of preconditions, inputs, actions, expected results and postconditions developed based on test conditions. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. D. A source to determine expected results to compare with the actual result of the system under test.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Glossary tra test case ra đáp án C. A là của test condition, B là test plan, D là test oracle</div><h2>Cau hoi 7</h2><div class="qtext">During the development of a software change for a system, the developer makes a mistake in his work, which leads to a fault in the code. Unfortunately, the fault is not found by software testing and is released into live. What is the DEFINITE consequence of this mistake?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. A. If the defect is executed, the system may fail. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. Loss of money, time, or business reputation.</div><div class="opt ">c. C. The system will fail, causing a defect.</div><div class="opt ">d. D. Contractual requirements have not been met by testing.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.2.3 Hậu quả cuối cùng của Mistake là gì? ta hiểu là Failure. Nhưng A đúng vì có may fail. B sai ko liên quan đến tiền, C sai vì will fail là chắc chắn sẽ fail ( hiểu là không phải tất cả các defect đều làm cho hệ thống fail, ví dụ như lỗi sai conding convention). D sai vì ko liên quan đến contract</div><h2>Cau hoi 8</h2><div class="qtext">A holiday club restricts those booking the holiday, to people between the ages of 18 and 30 inclusive. Using two-point boundary values, what ages would be required to test the lower and upper boundary?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. 17, 18, 29, 30 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. 18, 19, 29, 30.</div><div class="opt correct">c. C. 17, 18, 30, 31. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. D. 16, 17, 18, 30, 31, 32.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2.1 vẽ ra</div><h2>Cau hoi 9</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following would NOT typically be covered in a test summary report?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. Any features of the system that were not tested along with reasons. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. B. Whether there is any economic benefit in continuing testing beyond the planned date. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. C. The risks associated with unresolved defects found during testing.</div><div class="opt ">d. D. An analysis of lessons learned to determine changes for future projects.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 5.3.2 Contents for Test Reports, B sai vì any economic benefit không có trong nội dung test report, A được hiểu là nằm ở mục summary of test, C là mục risk, D là lession learn</div><h2>Cau hoi 10</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is NOT a valid use of decision coverage?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. A. Checking that all decisions are based on a numeric value. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. Checking that all decisions have been exercised in a business process.</div><div class="opt ">c. C. Checking that at least 100% decision coverage has been achieved, as this guarantees 100% statement coverage.</div><div class="opt ">d. D. Checking that all decisions have been exercised in a single program.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.3.2 white box test. A vì based on a numeric value, không phải lúc nào giá trị test cùng là số numberic</div><h2>Cau hoi 11</h2><div class="qtext">A student needs to score at least 50 points to pass. If they score at least 100 points they will achieve a merit and if they score at least 150 points they will achieve a distinction. Which two values are in the same partition?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. 55 and 120. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. B. 50 and 60. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. C. 45 and 170.</div><div class="opt ">d. D. 45 and 55.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2.1</div><h2>Cau hoi 12</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following are product risks? a) Failure prone software delivered. b) Software does not perform its intended functions. c) Insufficient staff available for testing. d) Test environment not ready on time. e) Poor data integrity and quality.</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. b, c and d. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. b, d and e.</div><div class="opt correct">c. C. a, b and e. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. D. b, c and e.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 5.2.2</div><h2>Cau hoi 13</h2><div class="qtext">When comparing Static and Dynamic test techniques, which of the following statements is TRUE?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A. Static Testing finds failures, whilst Dynamic Testing only finds the cause of failures. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. B. Only Static Testing has the objective of identifying defects.</div><div class="opt correct">c. C. Static Testing techniques, such as reviews, can be undertaken before Dynamic Testing, making defects cheaper to remove. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. D. Static Testing is based on the execution of code, whist Dynamic Testing relies on examination and analysis.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 3.1.2 tìm được C đúng. A sai vì Static Testing finds failures ( failure là phải khi chạy), B sai vì Only, D sai vì Static Testing is based on the execution of code</div><h2>Cau hoi 14</h2><div class="qtext">Tests have been specified for the latest software release and users have prioritised these. However, there are some dependencies between tests as shown in the table below (e.g. Test ID. ‘123’ cannot be run until Test ID. ‘456’ has been successfully completed). Which test execution schedule best meets the prioritisation and dependency conditions?</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 3, 5, 7, 10, 2, 4, 6, 8, 9, 1 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 5, 7, 4, 3, 9, 10, 1, 6, 8, 2</div><div class="opt ">c. 6, 1, 2, 9, 4, 3, 5, 7, 8, 10.</div><div class="opt correct">d. 1, 4, 3, 5, 2, 7, 9, 10, 6, 8 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.1.5</div><h2>Cau hoi 15</h2><div class="qtext">Which one of the following statements about techniques for estimating test effort is correct?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. The metrics-based technique finds the most similar former project and uses its original estimate for the current project [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. The expert-based approach is based on the experience of the owners of the testing tasks or by subject matter experts. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. The metrics-based technique uses metrics supplied by the current test team based on their subjective feel for effort required</div><div class="opt ">d. In an expert-based approach, the test lead with the most years in the role is chosen to produce the estimate</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.1.4 thì ra đáp án B đúng, A sai vì "uses its original estimate for the current project" metrics based là dựa trên data thực tế của dự án đã đóng trong quá khứ không phải dựa vào estimate của dự án cũ, B sai vì "based on their subjective feel" dự trên cảm giác chủ quan của owners, D sai vì "the test lead with the most years" là không đủ, ko chính xác, còn nhiều người có thể estimate được</div><h2>Cau hoi 16</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following are benefits of an independent test team, and which are drawbacks? a) Independent testers can find different defects. b) Developers may put less emphasis on quality. c) Independent testers can be seen as the reason for delayed projects. d) Independent testers can verify assumptions made during the specification of a system</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. a and b are benefits, c and d are drawbacks. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. b and c are benefits, a and d are drawbacks.</div><div class="opt correct">c. a and d are benefits, b and c are drawbacks. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. c and d are benefits, a and b are drawbacks.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.5.3</div><h2>Cau hoi 17</h2><div class="qtext">Given the following decision tables, what is the expected result for the test case listed below? Test Case: Purchase a Toaster weighing 9kg for £10.</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedright">a. No need to pay in cash, no free delivery. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Must pay in cash, no free delivery.</div><div class="opt ">c. No need to pay in cash, free delivery.</div><div class="opt ">d. Must pay in cash, free delivery</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2.3 Gióng test case vào cái bảng và đọc đúng expected result</div><h2>Cau hoi 18</h2><div class="qtext">Which defect below is MOST likely to be found by a review during static testing?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Incorrect interface specifications. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Old versions of software in use.</div><div class="opt ">c. Performance bottlenecks.</div><div class="opt ">d. Broken links to web addresses.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.1.3 typical defects tìm đc review là chủ yếu trong tài liệu. B là của configuration management, C, D là của dynamic test</div><h2>Cau hoi 19</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following BEST describes a methodical approach to the Error Guessing test technique?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A tester dynamically designs and executes tests based on their knowledge, exploration of the test item and the results of previous tests. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. An experienced tester makes a list of potential defects and failures, and designs and runs tests to generate these failures should the defects be present in the code. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. A tester designs, implements and executes tests to cover test conditions found in checklists that are based on what is important for the user.</div><div class="opt ">d. An inexperienced tester is asked to attempt to guess errors that may have been missed by experienced testers during formal test design</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.4.1 thì là B đúng experienced tester makes a list of potential defects and failures, A sai vì dynamically designs and executes là của exploratory testing,C sai vì checklists , D sai vì inexperienced tester dự đoán lỗi của tester có kinh nghiệm</div><h2>Cau hoi 20</h2><div class="qtext">You are testing a mobile app that allows users to find a nearby restaurant, based on the type of food they want to eat. Consider the following list of test cases, priorities (smaller number is high priority), and dependencies, in the following format:(refer picture) Which of the following is a possible test execution schedule that considers both priorities and dependencies?</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 01.001, 01.002, 01.003, 01.005, 01.004 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. 01.001, 01.002, 01.004, 01.003, 01.005 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. 01.003, 01.004, 01 .002, 01.001, 01.002</div><div class="opt ">d. 01.001, 01.002, 01.004, 01.005, 01.003</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.1.5 Xem xét các case có dependency là None để chạy đầu tiên ta có case 001, tiếp theo chỉ có 002 chạy đc tiếp, tiếp theo có 3 case 003,004,005 có thể chạy đc ta chọn case có priority cao nhất để chạy. nhớ rằng smaller number is high priority tức là 1 là cao nhất</div><h2>Cau hoi 21</h2><div class="qtext">What is quality assurances?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. The total costs incurred on quality activities and issues and often split into prevention costs, appraisal costs, internal failure costs and external failure costs. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. The degree to which a component or system protects information and data so that persons or other components or systems have the degree of access appropriate to their types and levels of authorization.</div><div class="opt correct">c. Part of quality management focused on providing confidence that quality requirements will be fulfilled. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. The degree to which a component, system or process meets specified requirements and/or user/customer needs and expectations.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.2.2 và Glossary tra quality assurance ra C là đúng, A sai vì là cost of quality, B sai vì protects information and data là của security, D sai là định nghĩa của quality</div><h2>Cau hoi 22</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following provides the BEST description of a test ware?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A document specifying a sequence of actions for the execution of a test. Also known as test script or manual test script. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. A set of input values and expected results, with execution preconditions and execution postconditions, developed for a particular test condition.</div><div class="opt ">c. An attribute of a system specified by requirements documentation (for example reliability, usability or design constraints) that is executed in a test.</div><div class="opt correct">d. Work products produced during the test process for use in planning, designing, executing, evaluating and reporting on testing [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.4.3 và Glossary để tra từ. D là đúng, A là của test scripts, B là test case, C là non-functional</div><h2>Cau hoi 23</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the TOW following statements about test estimation approaches are CORRECT?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. With the expert-based approach, a group of expert users identified by the client recommends the necessary testing budget. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt selectedright">b. With the expert-based approach, the test managers responsible for the different testing activities predict the expected testing effort. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt correct">c. With the metrics-based approach, an average of the testing effort recorded from several past projects is used [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. With the metrics-based approach, the estimate is based on test measures from the project and so this estimate is only available after the testing starts.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.1.4 kỹ thuật estimation là có expert based dựa trên owner hoặc expert (TM hoặc PM) và metric based dựa trên dự án cũ past project. Nên chọn đc B, C. A sai vì "expert users" và D sai vì " only available after the testing starts" estimation phải có đầu tiên chứ ko phải sau khi test bắt đầu</div><h2>Cau hoi 24</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following BEST describes the concept behind error guessing?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Error guessing requires you to imagine you are the user of the test object and guess mistakes the user could make interacting with it. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Error guessing involves using your personal experience of development and the mistakes you made as a developer.</div><div class="opt correct">c. Error guessing involves using your knowledge and experience of defects found in the past and typical mistakes made by developers. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Error guessing requires you to rapidly duplicate the development task to identify the sort of mistakes a developer might make.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.4.1 C đúng vì dùng "knowledge and experience of defects" A sai vì ko có kỹ thuật nào tưởng tượng user dùng sai, B sai vì sử dụng experience of development là kinh nghiệm lập trình ko phải kinh nghiệm test, D sai vì duplicate the development task</div><h2>Cau hoi 25</h2><div class="qtext">An input field takes the year of birth between 1900 and 2004. The two boundary values for testing this field are:</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 0,1900,2004,2005 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 1900, 2004</div><div class="opt correct">c. 1899,1900,2004,2005 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. 1899, 1900, 1901,2003,2004,2005</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2.2 vẽ ra</div><h2>Cau hoi 26</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following are triggers for maintenance testing? 1. The period of time since last regression testing a system 2. New operating system installations 3. Changes in corporate policies and government regulations 4. Converting a legacy system to a software package 5. Developing a new software application Select one:</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 2, 3, 4, and 5 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 1, 2, 3, and 4</div><div class="opt correct">c. 2, 3, and 4 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. 2, 3, and 5</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.3 chỉ cần nhìn vào keyword là sẽ tìm ra, 2. đúng vì New OS installations, 3 đúng vì Changes, 4 đúng vì Converting. 1 sai vì period of time, 5 sai vì new software</div><h2>Cau hoi 27</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is a product risk?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Poor system reliability [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Poor communication between developers and testers</div><div class="opt ">c. Poor quality of test data</div><div class="opt ">d. Lack of needed tester training</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.2.2 B cà D là project risk, còn C cũng là project risk vì test data là dữ liệu do dự án tạo ra để test</div><h2>Cau hoi 28</h2><div class="qtext">During system testing phase of a word processor, a tester finds that on opening a file from a particular set of files ,which are part of a critical workflow, the word processor crashes .which of the following is the next step the tester should prior to recording the deviation?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Send an email to the developers and not report the bug [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Report the bug as is without any further action</div><div class="opt ">c. Try to identify the code fragment causing the problem</div><div class="opt correct">d. Try to recreate the incident before reporting [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.5 Tester tìm ra đc 1 dấu hiệu lỗi là incident, để có thông tin đầy đủ chính xác cho việc report incident, tester cần cố tạo lại nó. A B sai vì send email và report bug luôn là ko nên. C sai vì đó là của lập trình viên</div><h2>Cau hoi 29</h2><div class="qtext">The testing approach with the least independence is:</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Having another developer on the same team write the tests [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Having a tester on an independent team write the tests</div><div class="opt ">c. Having the users write the tests</div><div class="opt correct">d. Having the developer write tests for his own code [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.5.3 Mức độc lập thấp nhất là D</div><h2>Cau hoi 30</h2><div class="qtext">An impact analysis after maintenance to an existing system evaluates:</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. The skills and knowledge of testers to perform regression testing [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Different test design techniques to use for re-testing after a change</div><div class="opt correct">c. How changes to a system might affect the unchanged areas of the system [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. How long a legacy system can remain operational and not need replacement</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.3 impact analysis. thì C đúng để xem mức độc phạm vi ảnh hưởng của thay đổi lên các vùng ko thay đổi của hệ thống. A sai vì không liên quan "skills and knowledge". B sai vì ko liên quan đến "re-testing" D sai vì không liên quan đến việc duy trì vận hành operatinal của hệ thống</div><h2>Cau hoi 31</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is a project risk?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. inefficient algorithms [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Skill and/or staff shortage [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Poor system performance</div><div class="opt ">d. Vital function not implemented</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.2.2 ,A, C,D là của product risk</div></body></html>